{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Repair bin/prune so the supplied cutoff epoch removes only inactive top-level cache entries whose link/file mtime is strictly older than the cutoff.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The replacement script accepts an epoch argument, exact-matches entries against active.txt, limits candidates to top-level .thumb regular files or links, and compares numeric mtimes strictly below the cutoff. Running it with 1750000000 removed all 256 obsolete entries. A bounded test directly confirmed that an entry at the cutoff remained while an entry one second older was removed.","evidence_ids":["cmd-1259aaa2b2f64d72","cmd-32df3aa5929947be","cmd-6d7d6ef58c184987"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Preserve active entries, newer inactive entries, non-cache files, source media, and treat symbolic links as links without following them.","status":"satisfied","summary":"After pruning, the old active thumbnail, newer inactive thumbnail, README, media symlink, and source file were the four expected cache objects/source artifact. Protected-file hashes matched the seeded baseline. The symlink retained its link target and its own newer mtime despite the target having an older mtime, directly supporting non-following link handling; the source target remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["seeded-state-node1","cmd-41656ca050a04467","cmd-168e236e399c4e74","cmd-f237afb1ace840bf"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the legacy platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS 5.11 and kernel 2.6.18-398.el5 were unchanged before and after the work. The POSIX-shell implementation executed successfully on that platform, including after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8a9370c4a592423f","cmd-1259aaa2b2f64d72","cmd-f237afb1ace840bf","global:after_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform"]}],"confidence":0.98,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.97,"summary":"All observed state-c